      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The accessory spleen is often a incidental discovery. The accessory post-accidental spleen are unusual. The torsion of a movable spleen is possible and represent about 0.2 to 0.3% of splenectomy. But the torsion of an accessory spleen is exceptional. A case of acute torsion of an accessory spleen is reported. In a 26-year-old women was admitted with acute abdominal pain. The abdominal ultrasound and the abdominal X-Ray are no specific. In the face of the acute pain, a laparoscopy was necessary. At laparoscopy, the patient was found to have torsion and infarction of an accessory spleen in the pelvis. The treatment was a splenectomy and the evolution was favorable."},
